lisa-design:
- Models live in relational/ssp_scope.go; normalization, hashing, limits and the service in relational/sspscope (Normalize is the single entry point for labels).
- Normalize also rejects keys containing "=" and keys/values containing control characters: MatchHash joins "key=value" pairs with "\n", so those characters would let two different entries share a hash. Small addition to the design's validation rules.
- Length limits count characters (runes), not bytes.
- Scope FKs (ON DELETE CASCADE to system_security_plans) are added by relational.EnsureSSPScopeConstraints, called from both migrators: AutoMigrate runs with DisableForeignKeyConstraintWhenMigrating, so the gorm constraint tags alone are not enforced.
- ToFilter collapses single-element levels (1 label -> condition, 1 entry -> that entry) and orders entries by MatchHash so the same scope always yields the same filter (A4 rewrites stored filters from it).
- afterChange runs only when the entry set changes (AddEntry, AddException that removed an entry, Learn that added entries); DeleteException does not change the scope.
- Learn fails the whole call with ErrLimitExceeded when the new entries would pass MaxEntries, rather than silently truncating; invalid labels fail the call too.
- Every write checks the SSP exists (ErrSSPNotFound) inside the locked transaction.

